# Question 3.14

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 1](assets/lect05e-probability_problems/image_001.png)

=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 1](assets/lect05e-probability_problems/image_001.png)

@right

- [Ab gamete]{color=red}
- 50% AABB &rarr; 0% chance of Ab
- 50% AABb &rarr; 50% chance of Ab
- [Multiplication rule]{color=orange}\:
- [50% x 0% = 0%]{color=orange}
- [50% x 50% = 25%]{color=orange}
- [Addition rule]{color=blue}\:
- [25% + 0% = 25% chance of Ab gamete]{color=blue}

=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 1](assets/lect05e-probability_problems/image_001.png)

@right

- [AB gamete]{color=green}
- 50% AABB &rarr; 100% chance of AB
- 50% AABb &rarr; 50% chance of AB
- [Multiplication rule]{color=orange}\:
- [50% x 100% = 50%]{color=orange}
- [50% x 50% = 25%]{color=orange}
- [Addition rule]{color=blue}\:
- [25% + 50% = 75% chance of AB gamete]{color=blue}

=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 1](assets/lect05e-probability_problems/image_001.png)

@right

- 25% chance of Ab gamete
- 75% chance of AB gamete
- Can they produce other gametes?
- [No]{color=red}
- [Good, because 25% + 75% = 100%!]{color=blue}

